 a word (captured in group 1), followed by one or more spaces, followed by the *exact same word* again. So it would match \"hello hello\" or \"foo foo\", but not \"hello world\".\n\nIn practice:\n- The pattern `(\\w+)` captures a word into group 1\n- `\\s+` matches spaces\n- `\\1` refers back to whatever was in group 1\n- `\\b` ensures word boundaries\n\nBackreferences are useful for finding duplicates, enforcing matching patterns (like opening/closing tags), or validating symmetry in text.","ttft_ms":2430,"type":"result","duration_ms":4547,"uuid":"2924d412-81d0-4675-bc18-ff044ea4c0c6","ttft_stream_ms":737,"time_to_request_ms":122,"first_content_frame_ms":737,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":383,"cacheReadInputTokens":6899,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0026149,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":156,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-12T05:14:51.381Z"}